cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Manacitra or its data, please cite it as below."
title: "Manacitra: a map of a quantum processor's qubit pairs"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Anish
    family-names: Patel
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-05
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/dogmaguru/manacitra"
abstract: >-
  Manacitra measures, for each qubit pair on a processor, how much of a small,
  known difference between two short circuits the pair keeps, and uses the
  resulting map to choose pairs for a job. The archived data (CC BY 4.0) are
  the per-pair counts from runs on two IBM processors and from simulations.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - qubit pairs
  - two-qubit gates
  - calibration
  - Qiskit
